I moved the conditional deep copies into the member-initializer list so each pointer is initialized directly to either a copied object or `nullptr`, eliminating the redundant null stores and branch bodies. This preserves identical behavior while giving the compiler a simpler, more optimizable constructor.

```cpp
DeveloperFieldDefinition::DeveloperFieldDefinition(const DeveloperFieldDefinition& other)
    : num( other.num )
    , size( other.size )
    , developerDataIndex( other.developerDataIndex )
    , mesg( other.mesg ? new FieldDescriptionMesg( *other.mesg ) : nullptr )
    , developer( other.developer ? new DeveloperDataIdMesg( *other.developer ) : nullptr )
{
}
```